 "notes": "Pseudoscalar (ALP) bosonic dark matter absorption limit via the axioelectric effect, digitised from the black observed XENON1T (this work) curve in Fig. 10 (top), g_ae vs m_a. Extracted as vector paths from Plot/alp_limit.pdf in the arXiv e-print (path item 180, width 1.75 black stroke), calibrated on the log-log axis tick labels (x: m_a in keV/c^2, converted to eV by x1000; y: g_ae). 90% C.L. Local sensitivity-loss spikes near 41.5 keV and 164 keV (83mKr and 131mXe backgrounds) are retained. Dark-matter density assumption rho~0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Sec. II C, Eq. 12); reported at the paper native density without rescaling. The paper also reports a vector (dark photon) kinetic-mixing chi limit (Fig. 10 bottom) and solar-axion 3D confidence surface; the ALP g_ae DM limit is chosen as the axion-electron main result. Note the paper observes a low-energy excess but sets these upper limits since no >3 sigma global significance for a peak.",
